Article 28
(1) The Gampong Government supports efforts to protect women by:
a. issuing gampong-level regulations on the protection of women;
b. socializing regulations related to the empowerment and protection of women to the community;
c. encouraging the realization of a gampong environment that is friendly towards women;
d. building community awareness including customary leaders and religious leaders at the gampong level to care about issues of violence against women;
e. allocating budget to support women's empowerment and protection programs; and
f. establishing a system for handling violence against women at the gampong level.
(2) The efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e, above can be developed in accordance with the gampong's financial capacity, problems and needs of women.

